# Shared checkout · clean worktree

**Invariant:** `shared_attended_checkout ⇒ branch ∈ {master, current_unchanged}` ·
`needs(feature_branch ∨ review_branch ∨ land_isolate) ⇒ git worktree add (clean)` ·
`¬git checkout(other_branch) on the shared tree` ·
`sole_maintainer_local ⇒ ¬push ∧ ¬pr` unless the operator names push / PR / publish.

Switching the shared tip for side work steals it from peer WIP. Lane B already
worktrees; attended seats owe the same. "Submit for review" ⇒ local branch +
`git diff --stat <base>..HEAD` — not `git push` / `gh pr create`.

## Forbidden / Required

| Forbidden | Required |
|---|---|
| `git checkout` / `switch` onto a side branch on the shared tree | `git worktree add [-b <branch>] <path> <start>`; work there |
| Stash to free the shared tip | Leave peer dirt; worktree isolates |
| `git push` / `gh pr create` / ask to open a PR | Local `@sha` + diffstat; land when told |

## Detents

- Tip already not `master`: ¬ force-switch mid-turn unless named; ¬ switch further for new side work — worktree from the start-point.
- Trivial same-tip edit on current shared branch: stay; worktree optional.
- `lane=B`: substrate worktrees suffice; ¬ move the shared IDE checkout.

## Land (attended)

```
shared tip stays master → worktree -b land/<slug> → commit → merge into master → remove worktree
```

No-PR removes the remote step, not the worktree.

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Switch shared tip to `fix/…`, amend, switch back | Worktree from `master`; merge back |
| Push / PR because a brief said "submit for review" | Local branch + diff; wait for land |

